                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">12. ARG

A variable that can be provided at build time is defined by an ARG Instruction. Once it has been
specified in the Dockerfile, you can specify it using the --build-arg switch when creating the image.
The Dockerfile supports multiple ARG instructions. The only instruction in the Dockerfile that can
come before the FROM instruction is ARG.

After the image is created, ARG values are not accessible. An ARG variable value won&#x27;t be accessible
to a running container.

Example

ARG image_name=latest

FROM centos:$image_name

docker build -t &lt;image-name&gt;:&lt;tag&gt; --build-arg image_name=centos8 .</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    

